{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TensorTraceCharacter","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TensorTraceCharacter","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.OrbitQuotientCount"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_permMatrixOf_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_permMatrixOf_two","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorTraceCharacter.lean#L140-L146","doc":"The `card κ = 2` specialisation, in the exact shape `ClassicalTraceFloor` assumes:\nthe `q = 1` Markov trace of a braid word is `2^{c(σ)}` before the `2^{-n}`\nnormalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_permMatrixOf_indexPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_permMatrixOf_indexPerm","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorTraceCharacter.lean#L125-L138","doc":"**The permutation character on a tensor power, as an actual matrix trace.**\n\n`σ` permuting the factors of `V^{⊗α}` with `V` free of rank `card κ` acts on the\nmonomial basis by the permutation `indexPerm σ κ`; its matrix is a permutation matrix\nand its trace is `(card κ) ^ orbitCount σ`.\n\nAt `card κ = 2` this is the `2^{c(σ)}` of `ClassicalTraceFloor`'s step 1 — now a\ntrace, not a count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_permMatrixOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_permMatrixOf","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorTraceCharacter.lean#L115-L123","doc":"**The trace of a permutation matrix is its number of fixed points.** The Mathlib\nequivalent is `Matrix.trace_permutation`; reproved here to avoid its import cone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.permMatrixOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.permMatrixOf","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorTraceCharacter.lean#L109-L113","doc":"The matrix of a permutation of basis vectors. Defined here rather than imported —\nsee the module docstring: Mathlib's `permMatrix` drags in a C*-algebra cone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.card_filter_fixed_indexPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.card_filter_fixed_indexPerm","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorTraceCharacter.lean#L97-L107","doc":"**The number of fixed monomial basis vectors is `(card κ) ^ orbitCount σ`.**\nThe combinatorial half of the trace computation — this is where\n`orbitCount_invariant_functions` enters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.indexPerm_fixed_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.indexPerm_fixed_iff","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorTraceCharacter.lean#L83-L95","doc":"A monomial basis vector is fixed by `σ` exactly when its index function is\nconstant on each cycle — i.e. exactly the invariant functions counted in\n`OrbitQuotientCount`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.indexPerm_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.indexPerm_apply","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorTraceCharacter.lean#L79-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.indexPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.indexPerm","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorTraceCharacter.lean#L73-L76","doc":"`σ` permuting tensor factors acts on the monomial basis `α → κ` by precomposition.\nThis is the index-level shadow of `PiTensorProduct.reindex`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}